@startuml
!include ../../../../../../plantuml/sodexo-theme.puml

title Select accommodation — Choose destination and search
header Sat, 25 Jul 2026 · End-to-end discovery sequence
footer (c) Developed by <b>Mohit Kanwar</b>

hide footbox
autonumber
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 90

actor "Traveller" as Actor
participant "Sodexo B2C Accommodation Lego" as Surface
participant "API Gateway" as Gateway
participant "Accommodation Experience API" as Edge
participant "Accommodation Service" as Service1
database "Service-owned data" as Data
queue "Kafka event platform" as Events
participant "Booking.com Demand API" as BookingCom #FBDADD


group 1. Return corporate sites and destinations allowed by the effective policy.
  Actor -> Surface: Return corporate sites and destinations allowed by the effective policy
  Surface -> Gateway: GET /api/v1/destinations?eligibleFor=me
  Gateway -> Edge: JWT, tenant scope, correlation ID
  Edge -> Service1: Return corporate sites and destinations allowed by the effective policy.
  alt authorised and valid
  Service1 -> Service1: Authorise and query
  Service1 -> Data: Read or commit Accommodation Service data
  Service1 --> Edge: Scoped result
  Edge --> Surface: Response envelope
  Surface --> Actor: Updated journey state
else validation, state, or dependency failure
  Service1 --> Edge: Problem details + retryability
  Edge --> Surface: Safe error and next action
  Surface --> Actor: Correct, retry later, or escalate
end
end

group 2. Search policy-aware accommodation inventory for a destination and stay.
  Actor -> Surface: Search policy-aware accommodation inventory for a destination and stay
  Surface -> Gateway: POST /api/v1/accommodations/search
  Gateway -> Edge: JWT, tenant scope, correlation ID
  Edge -> Service1: Search policy-aware accommodation inventory for a destination and stay.
  alt authorised and valid
  Service1 -> Service1: Authorise and query
  Service1 -> BookingCom: POST /3.2/accommodations/search
  BookingCom --> Service1: Supplier response + request_id
  Service1 --> Edge: Scoped result
  Edge --> Surface: Response envelope
  Surface --> Actor: Updated journey state
else validation, state, or dependency failure
  Service1 --> Edge: Problem details + retryability
  Edge --> Surface: Safe error and next action
  Surface --> Actor: Correct, retry later, or escalate
end
end

@enduml
